Z||000000||ray b||01-07-2001||06:41 PM|||| will you pay more for a 5spd or auto how much more if same cond mls. thinking of good to great lower mls car esp. 88. as poor cond prices should be low anyway.||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||01-07-2001||08:22 PM||||It depends on what the person wants. I prefer a five speed to the automatic and would pay more for a five seed. Other people would pay more for an automatic.<P>It also depends on what the person is going to use the car for. If it's a daily driver that he/she uses to get to work than chances are they will want an automatic. If its someone who is looking for a second car/toy who wants more sport in there driving and they don't depend on this car to get then to work than they may want the 5-speed.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fformula88||01-07-2001||08:24 PM||||AS a general rule the auto's tend to get more money.  Since the auto transmissions tend to be extra cost options on most cars, they raise the value.  <P>As far as a Fiero goes, I am not sure how much of a difference it makes.  I guess it depends on how much people are willing to pay for one over the other.  But since most Fieros don't have very high resale values anyway (aside from the $20K Fiero we have a thread on) I wouldn't expect it to make a big difference.<P>------------------<BR>John<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">    <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1997 Ford Probe SE<BR>AOL IM: Fformula88||||reg||1
